  "final_answer": "Apple's top Max chip for the 16-inch MacBook Pro is the **M5 Max**, and the highest-end version of it is the **18-core CPU / 40-core GPU** configuration (with a 16-core Neural Engine).\n\nIn that chip's standard memory and storage configuration — **48GB of unified memory and 2TB of storage** (48GB is the minimum memory Apple offers with the 40-core GPU, and 2TB is the base storage) with the standard display — the 16-inch MacBook Pro is priced at **$4,999.00** (or $416.58/month for 12 months with Apple Card Monthly Installments). Apple's order summary for that build lists: 16-inch MacBook Pro in Space Black, M5 Max chip, 18-core CPU, 40-core GPU, 16-core Neural Engine, 48GB unified memory, 2TB storage, Standard display, 140W Power Adapter.\n\nThe $150 nano-texture display, larger memory (64GB or 128GB), and larger storage (up to 8TB) are optional upgrades that would raise the price above that figure. Note the lower-tier M5 Max (18-core CPU / 32-core GPU, 36GB memory) starts at $4,399 — choosing the 40-core GPU adds $300 and requires stepping up to 48GB of memory.",
